<!--
    The widget's one and only border: Radius.Card's 14dp corners and
    Stroke.Hairline's 1dp edge over MonoScheme.surface.

    One card, not four. The two buttons inside it are separated by hairline
    rules rather than given borders of their own — nesting a bordered box
    inside a bordered box is a texture this app's design system does not have
    anywhere, and at widget size it reads as clutter immediately.

    The stroke is `outline` (#464646), not the `outlineVariant` an in-app card
    uses. In the app a card sits on `background` and the fill difference does
    half the work of separating it; on a home screen it sits on an unknown
    wallpaper, where the edge is the only thing defining the shape and the
    quieter hairline disappears into the fill.

    The fill is 90% opaque, not solid. Enough wallpaper comes through to
    place the bar on the home screen rather than on top of it, and not
    enough to cost the glyphs any contrast.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="#E6202020" />
    <stroke android:width="1dp" android:color="#FF464646" />
    <corners android:radius="14dp" />
</shape>
